     "I6"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "The study is a task-based fMRI reappraisal experiment using negative and neutral images, with within-task regulation and viewing contrasts (I1-I5). However, the available full text and criterion-bearing tables do not demonstrate peak coordinates in a standard anatomical space for a group-level whole-brain voxelwise map; whole-brain effects are only referred to as being in unavailable supplementary Tables S3/Figures S5-S6 (I6 not demonstrated)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "24493837",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Original task-based fMRI study of adults using instructed increase/decrease reappraisal of visual IAPS images, with within-task regulation and viewing contrasts and reported coordinates. However, the functional acquisition used only 26 axial-oblique slices with 20% skip, indicating partial brain coverage; no accompanying whole-brain task map is demonstrated. Thus I6 is not met and E2 applies."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "24782800",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I6",
     "E2"
